Port HEVC: PR #44's h265.c on this base, plus the four sites it needs

HEVC now decodes bit-exact on the VE through stock ffmpeg. H.264 is
untouched and still 5/5 bit-exact.

    h01-640x480-main    PASS (va) bit-exact, ve+25
    h02-1280x720-main   PASS (va) bit-exact, ve+25
    h03-640x480-nowpp   MISMATCH (va) ve+2   <- known, see below

WHERE THIS COMES FROM. src/h265.c is taken verbatim from bootlin PR #44
(head c488d8df, "Kernel 6.18" by Cn8001), which ports HEVC to the
stabilized V4L2 stateless uAPI: V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_* names, the
flags-bitfield SPS/PPS/slice_params, a new h265_fill_decode_params(), and
the reference-picture-set restructure that maps VA-API's ReferenceFrames[]
into poc_st_curr_before/after[] and poc_lt_curr[]. That last part was the
only piece of this work with real design risk, and it is correct.

WHY NOT JUST USE PR #44. It cannot decode anything on cedrus -- H.264 or
HEVC -- because it is based on master and never had this branch's
format-ordering fix. Measured, both codecs fail identically:

    s_fmt type=1 (CAPTURE) 640x480 -> 16x16
    create_bufs type=1 ... index=0
    Unable to set format for type 2: Device or resource busy

That is not a missing feature. cedrus_s_fmt_vid_out() refuses an OUTPUT
format change once the CAPTURE queue has buffers, and says why in a
comment; and cedrus_try_fmt_vid_cap_p() *derives* the capture size from
the coded format, so asking for it first yields the 16x16 minimum. The
V4L2 stateless spec (Documentation/userspace-api/media/v4l/dev-decoder.rst,
"Initialization") mandates OUTPUT-coded-format first. This branch already
does that, in RequestCreateSurfaces2, which is why lifting h265.c onto it
works where #44 does not.

THE FOUR SITES h265.c NEEDED, all of them places our H.264-only patch had
stripped HEVC from, each found by a distinct failure rather than by
reading:

  meson.build   h265.c was not built at all -> dlopen: undefined symbol
                h265_set_controls.
  config.c      three of them: RequestCreateConfig refused the profile;
                RequestQueryConfigProfiles never advertised it; and
                RequestQueryConfigEntrypoints returned zero entrypoints,
                which is why vainfo silently omitted HEVC even after the
                first two were fixed.
  picture.c     four switches: the picture/slice/IQ-matrix buffer copies
                and the EndPicture dispatch to h265_set_controls.

THE CODED FORMAT WAS HARDCODED. surface.c had

    unsigned int pixelformat = V4L2_PIX_FMT_H264_SLICE;

so an HEVC stream set S264 on the OUTPUT queue, cedrus selected its H.264
codec ops, and the engine ran 25 times producing an all-zero frame -- mean
0.0, not tiled, not garbage, simply never written. It now comes from
driver_data->coded_pixelformat, recorded in RequestCreateConfig. It has to
live on driver_data because the format must be set before any buffer
exists, which is earlier than the context that knows the profile;
vaCreateConfig always precedes vaCreateSurfaces, so that is early enough.

KNOWN LIMITATIONS, both stated rather than hidden:

  * h03-640x480-nowpp stalls: "Timeout when waiting for media request"
    after 2-5 frames, reproducibly. It differs from h01 only by wpp=0 --
    identical NAL structure, one slice per frame -- and GStreamer decodes
    it bit-exact, so cedrus can. Something we send is wrong specifically
    when entropy_coding_sync is off. Not yet diagnosed.
  * HEVC scaling lists are not passed to the kernel. PR #44 dropped the
    iqmatrix handling from h265_set_controls and never sets
    V4L2_CID_STATELESS_HEVC_SCALING_MATRIX. Our vectors do not use scaling
    lists, so the gate does not see it.
  * Entry point offsets are still not passed. NOTE this corrects an
    earlier claim in this tree that h01/h02 would REQUIRE them: they pass
    bit-exact without. Entry points let a decoder start WPP substreams in
    parallel; a sequential decoder does not need them for correctness.

MPEG-2 remains unadvertised on purpose -- RequestCreateConfig still
refuses it, and advertising what vaCreateConfig rejects is worse than
advertising nothing.

